\hypertarget{cross-tool-clustering}{%
\subsection{Cross-Tool Clustering}\label{cross-tool-clustering}}

Accuracy and validity describe each tool separately, whereas clustering tests agreement about binding regions. For every complex, poses from all three tools were pooled without prefiltering on PoseBusters validity and clustered by ligand centroid. The cluster centre nearest the crystal ligand was treated as the recovered crystallographic region only when it fell within the prespecified 4 \angstrom{} centroid threshold defined in the Methods, so a nearest cluster lying beyond that distance does not count as a recovery. Twenty-one of the 303 complexes have no cluster close enough to the crystal ligand to count as the site at all, so they carry no recovered region and contribute no pose to any composition statistic below, while remaining in the denominator of every rate reported here and counting as non-reaches. It is the same threshold that sets the retrospective oracle ceiling reported later in this subsection. All three arms are the whole-protein pipelines used throughout this chapter, with AutoDock Vina rescored and re-ranked by gnina, DiffDock refined by smina and EquiBind refined by gnina, so no arm carries a crystal-derived search box into the comparison. Figure~\ref{fig:results-r4} reports recovery within the top-N ranked poses for individual tools and combinations, with the corresponding rates in Table~\ref{tab:results-cluster-recovery}.

